# Documented CVE exceptions, not a way to route around the gate (DECISIONS.md
# §4: blocking objective findings is only defensible when being wrong is
# rare — an undocumented blanket ignore would be exactly the gaming that
# section warns against). Trivy's vulnerability DB is live, not pinned to
# the image build, so this file starts empty — populate it as real findings
# turn up, one CVE ID per line, each with a comment explaining why it's
# not exploitable in this service's actual deployment shape (upstream
# unfixable, or the affected package/library is never invoked by the app).
# --ignorefile requires this file to exist even when empty — CI FATALs
# without it (found live, session 8).
